1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,569
December 1950.

2
00:00:02,789 --> 00:00:05,234
Thousands of US Marines are trapped in

3
00:00:05,234 --> 00:00:07,519
the frozen mountains of North Korea,

4
00:00:07,519 --> 00:00:09,061
at minus thirty degrees.

5
00:00:09,531 --> 00:00:11,293
There is only one road to the

6
00:00:11,293 --> 00:00:11,579
sea.

7
00:00:11,799 --> 00:00:13,184
And at Funchilin Pass,

8
00:00:13,184 --> 00:00:15,440
the Chinese have blown up the bridge

9
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:16,620
over a deep chasm.

10
00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:18,813
No bridge means no trucks,

11
00:00:18,813 --> 00:00:20,698
no guns, and no way out for

12
00:00:20,698 --> 00:00:21,506
the wounded.

13
00:00:21,976 --> 00:00:23,981
So the answer came from the sky.

14
00:00:24,201 --> 00:00:26,566
A new bridge was dropped by parachute,

15
00:00:26,566 --> 00:00:27,337
in sections.

16
00:00:27,807 --> 00:00:30,381
Enough pieces survived the fall for engineers

17
00:00:30,381 --> 00:00:31,546
to put it together,

18
00:00:31,546 --> 00:00:32,906
and the column crossed.

19
00:00:33,126 --> 00:00:34,513
By the 11th of December,

20
00:00:34,513 --> 00:00:36,731
the Marines reached the port of Hungnam.

21
00:00:37,201 --> 00:00:38,567
Would you have tried it?

22
00:00:38,787 --> 00:00:41,005
Comment below, and follow for more.

23
00:00:41,225 --> 00:00:43,107
The full story of Chosin is on

24
00:00:43,107 --> 00:00:43,849
the channel.

